GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 clause 1 the local government area is in the Greater Sydney Region` MEANS
    elem area `Schedule 1 the local government areas comprising the Greater Sydney Region`

§ `Schedule 3 Savings and transitional provisions`

-- src:895 | (1) Section 3 (II) of the Interpretation Act 1897 continues to apply to an Act enacted before the appointed day as if this Act had not been enacted.
-- src:896 | (2) In this clause—
-- src:897 | the appointed day means the day appointed and notified under section 2 (3).
@ref Schedule 3 clause 1 (src:895-897)
GIVEN `the day the Act was enacted` IS A DATE
      `the day appointed and notified under section 2 (3)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 1 section 3 (II) of the Interpretation Act 1897 continues to apply to the Act as if this Act had not been enacted` MEANS
    IF Day `the day the Act was enacted` LESS THAN Day `the day appointed and notified under section 2 (3)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:900 | An order in force immediately before the commencement of this Act under section 27 (III) of the Interpretation Act 1897 shall be deemed to be an order made under section 77 (3) of this Act.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 2 (src:900)
GIVEN `it is an order under section 27 (III) of the Interpretation Act 1897` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was in force immediately before the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 2 the order is deemed to be an order made under section 77 (3)` MEANS
    IF `it is an order under section 27 (III) of the Interpretation Act 1897` AND `it was in force immediately before the commencement of this Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:903 | Section 37 of the Interpretation Act 1897 continues to apply to an instrument made by virtue of section 37 (I) of that Act before the commencement of this Act as if this Act had not been enacted.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 3 (src:903)
GIVEN `it is an instrument made by virtue of section 37 (I) of the Interpretation Act 1897 before the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 3 section 37 of the Interpretation Act 1897 continues to apply to the instrument as if this Act had not been enacted` MEANS
    IF `it is an instrument made by virtue of section 37 (I) of the Interpretation Act 1897 before the commencement of this Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:906 | Section 41 of the Interpretation Act 1897 continues to apply to a regulation (within the meaning of that section) published in the Gazette before the commencement of this Act as if this Act had not been enacted.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 4 (src:906)
GIVEN `it is a regulation, within the meaning of section 41 of the Interpretation Act 1897, published in the Gazette before the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 4 section 41 of the Interpretation Act 1897 continues to apply to the regulation as if this Act had not been enacted` MEANS
    IF `it is a regulation, within the meaning of section 41 of the Interpretation Act 1897, published in the Gazette before the commencement of this Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:909 | A reference in any Act to the laying of a statutory rule before either or both Houses of Parliament includes a reference to the laying before either or both Houses of Parliament of a written notice of the making of the statutory rule, as referred to in section 40.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 5 (src:909)
GIVEN `it is a reference in an Act to the laying of a statutory rule before either or both Houses of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 5 the reference includes a reference to the laying of a written notice of the making of the statutory rule, as referred to in section 40` MEANS
    IF `it is a reference in an Act to the laying of a statutory rule before either or both Houses of Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:912 | Section 577 of the Local Government Act 1919 continues to apply to an ordinance (within the meaning of that Act) published in the Gazette before the commencement of this Act as if this Act had not been enacted.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 6 (src:912)
GIVEN `it is an ordinance, within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1919, published in the Gazette before the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 6 section 577 of the Local Government Act 1919 continues to apply to the ordinance as if this Act had not been enacted` MEANS
    IF `it is an ordinance, within the meaning of the Local Government Act 1919, published in the Gazette before the commencement of this Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:915 | (1) Section 13A, as inserted by the Interpretation Amendment Act 2006, is taken to have applied to any Act in force before the commencement of that section (and to have applied on and from the enactment of any such Act).
@ref Schedule 3 clause 7(1) (src:915)
GIVEN `it is an Act in force before the commencement of section 13A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 7(1) section 13A is taken to have applied to the Act, and to have applied on and from its enactment` MEANS
    IF `it is an Act in force before the commencement of section 13A` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:916 | (2) Nothing in subclause (1) affects any judgment or other order of a court or tribunal given or made before the commencement of that section.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 7(2) (src:916)
GIVEN `it is a judgment or other order of a court or tribunal given or made before the commencement of section 13A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 7(2) clause 7(1) affects the judgment or order` MEANS
    IF `it is a judgment or other order of a court or tribunal given or made before the commencement of section 13A` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:917 | (3) In particular, the Roads and Traffic Authority is bound by the Landlord and Tenant (Amendment) Act 1948 in relation to the property located at 67 Cromwell Street, Croydon Park for so long as that property is leased by that Authority to Mrs Jill McNamara (being the appellant in the appeal to the High Court in McNamara (McGrath) v Consumer Trader and Tenancy Tribunal[2005] HCA 55 (29 September 2005)).
@ref Schedule 3 clause 7(3) (src:917)
GIVEN `the body is the Roads and Traffic Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is the property located at 67 Cromwell Street, Croydon Park` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is leased by that Authority to Mrs Jill McNamara` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 7(3) the Authority is bound by the Landlord and Tenant (Amendment) Act 1948 in relation to the property` MEANS
    IF `the body is the Roads and Traffic Authority` AND `the property is the property located at 67 Cromwell Street, Croydon Park`
    THEN JUST `the property is leased by that Authority to Mrs Jill McNamara`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:920 | A certificate given under section 5 of the Reprints Act 1972 before the repeal of that Act by the Interpretation Amendment Act 2006 is taken, after that repeal, to be a certificate given under section 45D of this Act.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 8 (src:920)
GIVEN `it is a certificate given under section 5 of the Reprints Act 1972 before the repeal of that Act by the Interpretation Amendment Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 8 the certificate is taken, after the repeal, to be a certificate given under section 45D` MEANS
    IF `it is a certificate given under section 5 of the Reprints Act 1972 before the repeal of that Act by the Interpretation Amendment Act 2006` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:923 | (1) This clause applies to statutory rules and other instruments that were required to be published in the Gazette, but that are required (by amendments made by the Interpretation Amendment Act 2006, by a regulation under section 44 or by any other Act) to be published instead on the NSW legislation website.
-- src:924 | (2) In any Act or instrument, a reference to the publication in the Gazette of a statutory rule or other instrument to which this clause applies includes a reference to its publication on the NSW legislation website instead of its publication in the Gazette.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 9 (src:923-924)
GIVEN `it is a statutory rule or other instrument that was required to be published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is required, by amendments made by the Interpretation Amendment Act 2006, by a regulation under section 44 or by any other Act, to be published instead on the NSW legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 9 a reference to its publication in the Gazette includes a reference to its publication on the NSW legislation website instead` MEANS
    IF `it is a statutory rule or other instrument that was required to be published in the Gazette` AND `it is required, by amendments made by the Interpretation Amendment Act 2006, by a regulation under section 44 or by any other Act, to be published instead on the NSW legislation website` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:929 | (1) Section 21 (3), as inserted by the Crimes Legislation Amendment Act 2013, is taken to have applied to any Act in force before the commencement of that subsection (and to have applied on and from the enactment of any such Act).
@ref Schedule 3 clause 11(1) (src:929)
GIVEN `it is an Act in force before the commencement of section 21 (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 11(1) section 21 (3) is taken to have applied to the Act, and to have applied on and from its enactment` MEANS
    IF `it is an Act in force before the commencement of section 21 (3)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:930 | (2) Nothing in subclause (1) affects any judgment or other order of a court or tribunal given or made before the commencement of that subsection.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 11(2) (src:930)
GIVEN `it is a judgment or other order of a court or tribunal given or made before the commencement of section 21 (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 11(2) clause 11(1) affects the judgment or order` MEANS
    IF `it is a judgment or other order of a court or tribunal given or made before the commencement of section 21 (3)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:933 | (1) This clause applies to Acts printed by the Government Printer before the commencement of the Statute Law (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act (No 2) 2024.
-- src:934 | (2) The date purporting to be the date of assent, as appearing on the Act, is admissible in any legal proceedings as evidence of the date of assent to the Act.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 12(2) (src:933-934)
GIVEN `it is an Act printed by the Government Printer before the commencement of the Statute Law (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act (No 2) 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 12(2) the date purporting to be the date of assent, as appearing on the Act, is admissible in legal proceedings as evidence of the date of assent` MEANS
    IF `it is an Act printed by the Government Printer before the commencement of the Statute Law (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act (No 2) 2024` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:933 | (1) This clause applies to Acts printed by the Government Printer before the commencement of the Statute Law (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act (No 2) 2024.
-- src:934 | (2) The date purporting to be the date of assent, as appearing on the Act, is admissible in any legal proceedings as evidence of the date of assent to the Act.
-- src:935 | (3) All matters not forming part of the Act that are set out in the document containing the text of the Act are material that may be considered in the interpretation of the Act, or a statutory rule made under the Act, under section 34.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 12(3) (src:933-935)
GIVEN `it is an Act printed by the Government Printer before the commencement of the Statute Law (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act (No 2) 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 12(3) the matters not forming part of the Act that are set out in the document containing the text of the Act are material that may be considered under section 34` MEANS
    IF `it is an Act printed by the Government Printer before the commencement of the Statute Law (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act (No 2) 2024` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:936 | (4) In this clause—
-- src:937 | Government Printer means the Government Printer of New South Wales, and includes any other person authorised by or on behalf of the Government to print any Act or instrument or other document.
@ref Schedule 3 clause 12(4) (src:936-937)
GIVEN `it is the Government Printer of New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is another person authorised by or on behalf of the Government to print an Act or instrument or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 3 clause 12(4) the person is the Government Printer` MEANS
    `it is the Government Printer of New South Wales` OR `it is another person authorised by or on behalf of the Government to print an Act or instrument or other document`

